Source transitions, not deductions from a timeout alone:
* /114 func_19:184–197 supplies the unmodified int8 local 127 as func_47's
  uint64 p_50. Its label124 body (437–443) has no write/escape of that value.
  func_64's signed int16 -11 >= -8 loop is skipped; func_58's signed int8
  -25,-19,-13,-7 progression ends at -1. Both callees therefore return, and
  the unchanged nonzero parameter restarts the caller. Union member writes
  do not alias the parameter. Safe arithmetic helpers do not change this guard.
* /234 func_42:516–605 binds g_28 and l_157 to the same g_93[2] object. Once
  its != arm is reached, l_162[6]=8 and l_164[0][4]=0xa8 force its first arms.
  The only pointee update is OR with a Boolean; g_73 is not written. The inner
  unsigned-halfword loop runs 6,11,16 and stops at 21. A nonzero pointee breaks
  with g_68.f0=0; a zero pointee leaves g_68.f0=-4. Either leaves != true.
  Local l_194=3 restarts. No call or pointer store on this path changes the
  compared object identities. The fixture covers zero/positive/negative
  pointees, both comparison outcomes, and repeated transitions.
* /132 func_90:1052–1102 resets g_75=0; g_41=0 <= -18 skips all writes to
  g_107. Both stopped oracles observe g_107=0x4e86, g_75=g_41=0. The nonzero
  guard jumps back before increment; no call or live body mutates it.
* /54 func_15:781–907 runs a finite signed 19..-3 loop. g_324=0 >=25 skips
  its entire body, including every possible pointee write. Both oracles see
  g_6=6, g_324=0 and g_9 at different finite-loop positions. The following
  p_16=0 iteration jumps back on unchanged g_6. A finite inner loop alone
  would not explain the timeout; this caller-level restart does.
* /162 func_1:77–146 selects the zero comma result l_8, not the safe remainder.
  Its false arm sees unchanged local l_605=-6 and restarts before either
  induction update. The alternate arm's calls and writes are unreachable.
* /173 func_50:598–615 repeats its first p_54=0 iteration. Constant 0x3632e6ba
  OR forces the arm which copies g_85 only to a local; the sole guard-changing
  else is unreachable. func_58:623–690 resets g_17 to zero and returns at the
  first l_78 iteration after finite loops; it never modifies g_85. Both oracles
  observe the same 32-byte g_85 representation, with f3.f0=482. The fixture's
  target sizeof/offsetof and raw-byte checks independently verify that decoding.
* /206 func_11:404–421 resets g_278 and g_18.f3 to zero, copies a record to
